# Local-only development files.
#
# NOTE (2026-08-01): this block used to also exclude everything the build and
# the test suites actually need -- `/src-tauri/src/tests/`,
# `commands/data_tests.rs`, `commands/debug.rs`, `/src/test/`, `/e2e/`,
# `vitest.config.ts`, `playwright.config.ts`. The result was that the
# repository did not compile from a clean checkout at all:
# `commands/mod.rs` declares `pub mod debug;` unconditionally, and
# `historical_scan.rs`/`polling.rs` read `SCAN_QUEUE_PAUSED`/`GMAIL_POLL_PAUSED`
# from it on the live polling path, so `cargo build` failed with
# "file not found for module `debug`". `cargo test` additionally lost the
# phase8-11 suites and `data_tests.rs`; `npm test` lost its vitest config and
# `src/test/setup.ts`.
#
# rust.yml has been running `cargo test --all-features` and react.yml
# `pnpm test` on every push the whole time, so neither workflow can ever have
# succeeded -- the same failure mode the /scripts/* note below already records
# once, and the same one as the nightly benchmark job (audit_09 #8).
#
# Only machine-local scratch remains excluded. The former entries for
# `dev_review.rs`, `bin.rs` and `test_shutdown.sh` are gone because those
# files are gone -- an ignore rule for a file that no longer exists is a
# rule nobody can evaluate.
/playwright-report/
/scripts/*
# TASK-QA-010/OPS-001/OPS-008 finding: these three scripts are genuine CI
# dependencies -- release.yml runs security_hardening_check.sh and
# notarize.sh on every tagged release push, ci.yml runs
# verify_acceptance_criteria.py on every push/PR -- unlike the rest of
# /scripts/ (local-only dev tooling: DMG signing prep, backup/restore,
# rollback, that needs local credentials/interactive input CI never has).
# All three were previously gitignored along with everything else in this
# directory, meaning release.yml would have failed with "file not found" on
# the very first real tagged release (neither script has ever actually been
# in the repository despite being referenced by a workflow the whole time).
# Git can't re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded via a
# trailing-slash pattern (`/scripts/`), hence `/scripts/*` here instead --
# the standard "ignore all but these" idiom.
!/scripts/verify_acceptance_criteria.py
!/scripts/security_hardening_check.sh
!/scripts/notarize.sh
!/scripts/verify_release_prerequisites.sh
!/scripts/generate_release_notes.sh
!/scripts/.placeholder_license_public.pem.sha256
audit.md
fix-log.md
implementation-log.md
README.md
/docs/
.tokensave
*.db